    √ 3. Empty submission response updates lastSyncAt to prevent rapid polling spinning (3 ms)
    √ 4. Full idempotency on repeat sync with identical submissions (9 ms)
    √ 5. Foreign sample collision strictly avoids mutation, reports FOREIGN_SCOPE_COLLISION, and halts cursor (7 ms)
    √ 6. Duplicate branch enforces commit gates and rolls back transaction on revoked config (9 ms)
    √ 7. Conflict replay idempotency: repeating the conflicting submission does not append duplicate entries or duplicate audit rows (18 ms)
    √ 8. Case-insensitive lookup preserves evidence on lowercase existing record in DB, advancing cursor cleanly (8 ms)
    √ 9. Ambiguous depth identity retains a durable hold through physical arrival and blocks acceptance (36 ms)
    √ 10. Unchanged original primary replay causes zero metadata, audit, or hold changes (8 ms)
    √ 11. Cross-form occurrences with same kobo_id and depth are preserved and not silently deduplicated (13 ms)
    √ 12. Unknown ownership and historical samples (REJECTED/RECEIVED) are protected from mutation (7 ms)
    √ 13. Real isolated reception intake and consignment routes block AMBIGUOUS_PROVENANCE_HOLD with HTTP 409, while normal sample succeeds (50 ms)
    √ 14. SampleWorkspaceService blocks canAcceptIntake when AMBIGUOUS_PROVENANCE_HOLD is active (11 ms)
    √ 15. Source-B primary record does not suppress source-A submission with same ID and depth (Finding 1) (8 ms)
    √ 16. Primary occurrence replayed with changed coordinates or attachments creates revision hold (Finding 2) (12 ms)
    √ 17. Conflicting occurrence replayed with changed coordinates preserves revision append-only (16 ms)
    √ 18. Repeated revised-primary replay with identical revised evidence is idempotent (da8b561 review regression) (15 ms)
